_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Flowers Foods, Inc. produces and markets packaged bakery food products in the United States. The company's principal products include fresh breads, buns, rolls, snack items, bagels, English muffins, tortillas, baking mixes, and frozen breads and rolls as well as snack items including bars, cakes, cookies, and crackers. The company offers its products under the Nature's Own, DKB, Canyon Bakehouse, Simple Mills, Wonder, and Tastykake brand names. It distributes its products through a direct-store-delivery distribution and a warehouse delivery system, as well as operates bakeries. The company's customers include national and regional restaurants, institutions and foodservice distributors, and retail in-store bakeries; wholesale distributors; mass merchandisers, supermarkets, vending outlets, and convenience stores; quick-serve chains, food wholesalers, institutions, dollar stores, and vending companies; and public health care, military commissaries, and prisons, and other governmental institutions. The company was formerly known as Flowers Industries and changed its name to Flowers Foods, Inc. in 2001. Flowers Foods, Inc. was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in Thomasville, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. A. Ryals McMullian Jr. | CEO & Chairman of Board | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $510K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Flowers Foods, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.1B market cap on $5.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 6% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $319M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 19.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 59/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 31% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"There May Be Reason For Hope In Flowers Foods' (NYSE:FLO) Disappointing Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/food-beverage-tobacco/nyse-flo/flowers-foods/news/there-may-be-reason-for-hope-in-flowers-foods-nyseflo-disapp","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795200816.036,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.403,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Flowers Foods Implements Executive Severance Plan for Key Officers","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/flowers-foods-implements-executive-severance-plan-for-key-officers","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795615229.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Shaun Mara Awarded 18,890 Deferred Shares in Flowers Foods' 2026 Equity Plan","source":"kalkineme